    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "AIR PORT PILE•\nCITY OF SAN HAZSO, CALLPORILA,\nostice of City Clerke\nSeptember 8, 1926\nMAYOR JAMES ROLPH, Res ani\nBOARD OF SUPERVISORS,\nSan Franei soo, California.\nDeat Sins:\nPursuant to zesolution of the City Council of San lateo,\nthe undersigned as layor o1 the City, urges your serious considere-\ntion of the proposed aviation tield immediately adjoining San lateo\non the south for the use of San Francisco as a lunicipal Aviation\nFielde\nOur consideration of the matter convinces us that the proposed\nsite has many advantages which makes it far superior to any of the\nother proposed sites on the peninsula.\nWith an area of tive laundred acres available, with a length of\nover a mile and a half and a breath of practically a mile, and with\nan absolutely level surface, the landing and take-off possibilities\nare unexcelled.\nThe proposed site is located between the Iealie and Berestord\nstations on the main line of the Southern Pacifie Railway, with a\ntrain service in excess of tilty trains per day, and on the liain\nState Highway leading Iron San Froncisco to San Jose.\nThe olimatic and air conditions are extraordinarily good and\na portion of the proposed site has been used as an aviation field\nfor a number of yeazs.\nAviators inform us that absence of fog and\nwind make it possible\nto land on this site at any and all times,\nwhich would unquestionably offset the time consumed by the addi-\ntional distance fron San Francisco.\nThis field is innediatoly available and without grading or\nother improvement could be used immediately for aviation purposes.\nIt is also my understanding that the title to the property is in\nsuch a condition that the site can be imediately secured at a very\nreasonable price.\nThe proposed site is within a very short distance of the City\nof San lateo, which has under contemplation the annexation o2 the\nproperty imediately adjoining the proposed site, and so far as the\n810\n600 г",
